{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"Add a code-review **surface-parity** overlay: a Pass-1 specialist reviewer for the\nfour-pass code-review gate that flags when a write-op's parameter / guard / required-field\nsurface changes on ONE adapter (lib `_lib_writes.py`, CLI `_commands/`, MCP `_mcp_writes.py`)\nwithout the sibling surfaces being updated in lockstep. This is the STATIC code-review\ncomplement to the runtime behavioral conformance oracle already landed under\ntopaz-blubbery-mice: the oracle proves parity at test time; this overlay coaches an author (at\nreview time) toward parity BEFORE the code lands, catching the escaped-bug class recorded on\ncranial-goodly-seahog (a guard/arg added to one entry point and not mirrored to its siblings;\nworst case halfwhite-chordal-stonefly had 9 prior PASS reviews with zero findings).\n\nAdvisory-first (blocking_enabled=false): a divergence is a coach-not-block finding, verified in\nPass-2 and decided in Pass-3 like every other overlay. A DELIBERATE divergence the author\njustifies in the diff/commit must NOT fire (the reviewer prompt carries that false-positive\nguard).\n\n## Approach\n\nModel it on the existing GLOB-triggered overlays (api-compat, security): the overlay fires when\nthe diff touches a known write-surface adapter file, and the LLM reviewer judges whether an\nactual param/guard/required-field surface changed and whether the sibling adapters were updated\nin lockstep. No change to `registry.content_triggered_overlays` is needed (that scanner is for\nthe removed-decl deletion-impact trigger); glob routing via `applies_to` is the right, existing\nseam and keeps the overlay inert on unrelated diffs.\n\n1. New packaged reviewer prompt `src/rebar/llm/reviewers/code-review-surface-parity.md`\n   (front-matter `dimension: code-review-surface-parity`,\n   `langfuse_prompt: rebar-code-review-surface-parity`, `outputs: code_review_findings`,\n   `execution_mode: agentic`, `category: code-review-pass`), matching the deletion-impact /\n   api-compat prompt contract (evidence-record findings, `criteria: [\"surface-parity\"]`, no\n   model-emitted severity — Pass-3 computes it). The prompt enumerates the three write surfaces,\n   tells the reviewer to Grep the sibling adapters for the changed param/guard, and carries the\n   false-positive guards (deliberate justified divergence; a purely internal refactor that\n   changes no caller-visible surface; an adapter-bound param such as `_creation_channel` /\n   `return_alias` / `source` / `repo_root` that is intentionally not caller-visible).\n2. Register the overlay id: add `\"surface-parity\"` to `OVERLAY_IDS` in\n   `src/rebar/llm/code_review/registry.py` (closed enum; comment it as glob-triggered,\n   advisory).\n3. Add the routing entry to `src/rebar/llm/code_review/criteria_routing.json`:\n   `exec: AGENT`, `applies_to` globbing the write-surface adapters\n   (`**/_commands/**`, `**/_lib_writes.py`, `**/_mcp_writes.py`), `default_posture: advisory`,\n   `block_threshold: 0.95`, `blocking_enabled: false`, with a `_comment` citing this ticket.\n4. Regenerate the derived selection catalog `src/rebar/llm/reviewers/index.json` via\n   `prompts.regenerate_prompt_index()` so the new prompt is discoverable and the CI prompt-index\n   drift gate stays green.\n\n## Portability\n\nThe overlay is part of rebar's IN-PROCESS code-review gate (`rebar review-code` /\n`produce_code_review_verdict`); it is exercised by the same library entry point on every\nplatform and has NO dependency on any specific CI provider (it runs identically with a diverse\nCI provider or with no CI provider at all). The routing/registration is data + a packaged\nprompt, loaded in-process. This satisfies `project.portability`.\n\n## Scope\n\n- ADD `src/rebar/llm/reviewers/code-review-surface-parity.md` (new reviewer prompt).\n- EDIT `src/rebar/llm/code_review/registry.py` — append `\"surface-parity\"` to `OVERLAY_IDS`\n  (+ its explanatory comment). No other logic changes (glob routing + threshold_for already\n  handle a new id generically).\n- EDIT `src/rebar/llm/code_review/criteria_routing.json` — add the `surface-parity` entry.\n- REGEN `src/rebar/llm/reviewers/index.json` (mechanical, from the new prompt's front-matter).\n- ADD tests (see Testing).\n\nOUT OF SCOPE: flipping the overlay to blocking (advisory-first by design; a later calibration\nticket may promote it, mirroring cranial-goodly-seahog); any change to the runtime oracle\n(topaz); any change to the write adapters themselves (scratchy/blusterous own those).\n\n## Testing\n\n- Unit: assert `\"surface-parity\"` is a member of `OVERLAY_IDS` and that\n  `registry.routing_index()[\"surface-parity\"]` has the expected shape\n  (`exec == \"AGENT\"`, advisory, `blocking_enabled is False`, `block_threshold == 0.95`, and the\n  three write-surface globs present).\n- Unit: assert `registry.threshold_for([\"surface-parity\"])` resolves to `(0.95, False)`\n  (advisory, non-blocking) — it does NOT join the approved blocking set.\n- Unit: assert the glob routing FIRES the overlay for a changed\n  `src/rebar/_commands/transition.py` (and `_mcp_writes.py`) and stays inert for an unrelated\n  file (e.g. a docs-only change), via the existing overlay-selection seam\n  (`overlay_union` / `workflow_ops`).\n- Drift: assert the regenerated `reviewers/index.json` is byte-identical to\n  `prompts.regenerate_prompt_index()` output (the packaged prompt is registered) — i.e. the CI\n  prompt-index drift gate passes.\n- `make lint` + `make typecheck` green; the complexity ratchet unaffected (no function grows).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A new `surface-parity` overlay exists in the code-review gate: `\"surface-parity\"` is a\n      member of `OVERLAY_IDS` and has a routing entry in `criteria_routing.json`.\n- [ ] The overlay is GLOB-triggered on the three write-surface adapters\n      (`_commands/`, `_lib_writes.py`, `_mcp_writes.py`) and stays inert on unrelated diffs.\n- [ ] The overlay is ADVISORY (`blocking_enabled: false`, `block_threshold: 0.95`);\n      `threshold_for([\"surface-parity\"])` == `(0.95, False)` and it is NOT in the approved\n      blocking set.\n- [ ] A packaged reviewer prompt `code-review-surface-parity.md` exists (deletion-impact/api-\n      compat contract) and `reviewers/index.json` is regenerated so the prompt-index drift gate\n      passes.\n- [ ] The reviewer prompt carries the false-positive guards (deliberate justified divergence;\n      adapter-bound non-caller-visible params; internal-only refactors) so a compliant lockstep\n      change or a justified divergence returns no finding.\n- [ ] `make lint` + `make typecheck` pass and the new unit tests are green."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787116425213106001,"uuid":"6995431e-62f6-429d-8dc2-3703d5038faa"}